bump this file to build Poltergeist 2 on Brandon's Mac (and install it there)
build 1: Poltergeist 2 = the Poltergeist look on the Six Sines engine (upstream baconpaul/six-sines d6f9b15, engine unchanged)
build 2: VST3 + CLAP first; the standalone app after its menu nib (Brandon's Mac has no Xcode ibtool)
build 3: the checks find the build (it is a symlink on Brandon's Mac); the app's menu nib from the official Six Sines Mac release, renamed
build 4: link panel ENV AMT beside DEPTH / LFO AMT; sound-folder chips without MPE / MTS-ESP / Templates; the release check really releases
build 5: MORPH page - the blend board (four corners, the puck mixes the real sounds, volume + pan per corner, the spectrum)
build 6: MORPH automatable by the DAW (ON, X, Y, ORBIT, RATE, SIZE) + ORBIT (circle, figure 8, square, swing, drift) locked to the bars
build 7: SPECTRAL page - spectral effects after the engine (Spectral Corruptor's 38 effects in four slots + WarpCore spectral inversion), off = the sound exactly as before
build 8: the ghost-machine look - every page a hand-painted part of the flying machine (GHOSTS, MAIN, MORPH, FX with the ghost = Spectral Corruptor and the flying town = WarpCore); hoses make the FM links; storm and lightning; the old look stays in the code
build 8b: same as build 8, the checks keep a backtrace if they crash
build 8c: same as build 8, crash report kept if the checks crash
build 8d: build 8 with the checks' synth on the heap (they overflowed the Mac's 8 MB main-thread stack)
build 9: brass spyglass by the OUT gauge on every page opens the Six Sines analyzer (spectrum + scope) in a painted frame; drag the corner grip to resize the whole plugin
build 9b: spyglass colours - teal scope line, amber spectrum with a glow, Poppins labels, machine-style right-click menu (the analyzer works the same)
build 10: SUB - a sub-bass button (sign under VOICES by the OUT gauge, on every page) opens a SUB panel: Bombaz oscillator + Subhoofer harmonics under the lowest note, after the engine and SPECTRAL FX, MAKE ROOM low cut, 8 presets; SUB off = the sound exactly as before
build 11: fixes the crash on FFT 4096 (the restart after a new FFT size left the FX page reading a freed spectrum); the page-change cloud, cross-fade and rain show again at every window size; the SPYGLASS comes back in front of the plugin window after every press and release on the machine (it still moves on its own); bundle id io.ghostblock.poltergeist2
build 12: the BACK ROOM - click the ghost's eyes or mouth (GHOSTS, MAIN, MORPH) to go behind the machine: every FM link as plumbing, a window per link with its amount (click to plug in, drag for how much, right-click to unplug), feedback on the diagonal, YOU HEAR for the mix; FRONT PANEL or Esc goes back out; the front panel is unchanged
build 13: the checks keep their own settings file - your saved window size (108 %) was opening their test window at 1122 x 803, so every pointer check missed and build 12 never installed; the checks also no longer reset your saved size. Same Back Room as build 12
build 14: MORPH - every corner gets an OCTAVE window between VOLUME and PAN (-3 .. +3): top half = up, bottom half = down, wheel, right-click = the list; greyed while the corner is empty. Only the keys that corner's sound hears move (THIS SOUND moves only while MORPH is on); notes are let go where they were played (no stuck notes); saved with the project
build 15: STUDIO VIEW - a button top left on the machine swaps to a plain synth screen (preset bar, tabs, a column per ghost with its level envelope bars, RATIO / OCTAVE / FEEDBACK / PAN / WAVE / ENV AMT knobs and a VOLUME fader, a MAIN tab for the whole sound, a keyboard); WIRING opens the Back Room, MORPH / FX open those machine pages, MACHINE VIEW goes back; greyed when a control does nothing; remembers which view you used
build 16: STUDIO VIEW has everything - GHOSTS (with LEVEL / FB / PITCH envelopes), MAIN (envelope, voice, output, tone, drift / pitch drop, macros), WIRING (a grid of who haunts who + the chosen wire's controls), MORPH (corners, blend pad, orbit), FX (spectral rack + WarpCore), SUB (with presets); no more 'switch to the machine'. The way in is part of the picture now: a lit house window (GHOSTS, MAIN), the lighthouse lantern (FX), the sun (MORPH)
build 17: STUDIO VIEW - no BACK ROOM buttons; pages no longer 'get stuck' when switching tabs (the whole new page is put on the screen at once, not bit by bit as the pointer moves)
build 18: MORPH SETS - 12 ready-made blend boards in the corner ledger's first tab (four factory sounds that blend well: same envelope type and register, each corner's VOLUME / OCTAVE set so all four play equally loud, with ORBIT)
build 19: BLEND GUARD on MORPH - when the blended sounds cancel each other it flips one's phase (inaudible on its own) and holds each of 6 bands at the level the sounds should add up to, so the middle of the board no longer goes thin (or doubles up); the status slit says which corners were cancelling. A corner alone is untouched.
build 20: BLEND GUARD - a phase flip now waits for that sound's next silence (never mid-note: a flip in a note could thump on low sounds), and its level corrections glide slower while blending
